nodes.body:
Thanks for carrying #52628 over to this one. On lower concurrency: agreed. The `build()` saving is fixed per step (−14 to −15 µs per call, 3 calls/step on V4 and 7 on V4.1), so at concurrency 61 it disappears into a ~30 ms TPOT.

The next round will cover:
- concurrency 1 and 5, with and without DSpark;
- a null arm (this PR with the flag forced off), so the `build()` packing and the DSpark draft-update effect show up separately;
- draft acceptance next to GSM8K. A stale ragged buffer on the draft side would lower acceptance long before it shows up in accuracy, because verification keeps the target's greedy output either way.

The shared-helper refactor is in ec746e97f7, and the DSpark answer is in the inline thread.

